{sov: Notes}
Laurel Canyon Blues: Opening track from 1968's Blues From Laurel Canyon,
driven by Mick Taylor's classic guitar work and Mayall's harp and piano.

12-Bar Form: The tune follows a standard 12-bar shuffle blues layout in
Ab major.

Harmonica and Piano Interplay: The driving shuffle relies on the steady
rhythmic bounce between the piano left hand and harp accents.

Guitar Tone: Mick Taylor uses clean, biting Ab dominant 7th voicings and
pentatonic lead fills off the top-string shapes.
{eov}